{"type":"message","id":"584cb39c","parentId":"17de2847","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:10:31.328Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Actually I can't just send a link like that to re-authorize - OAuth flow requires user interaction. Let me try a different approach. Maybe there's a way to check if the feishu plugin has a built-in reauth mechanism. Let me look at the feishu tools more carefully.\n\nActually, let me try to check if there's a way to use the feishu app's batch auth tool. Looking at the docs reference from MEMORY.md, it mentioned `feishu_oauth_batch_auth`. Let me see if this is accessible through the exec tool somehow.\n\nWait - the issue is that the token is stored in macOS Keychain and hasn't been refreshed. \n\nThe plugin should be handling token refresh automatically when it gets a 401, so either it didn't detect the failure or the refresh endpoint isn't working as expected. Rather than continuing to troubleshoot this in the dark, I should ask the user directly what they mean by \"同意你需要的权利\" - whether they completed the authorization flow in the Feishu app or if they're expecting something else to happen.","thinkingSignature":"6211c0b228bfd21ead137ea198bef4fe5b833f112cea4544c2e796bfdebc6920"},{"type":"text","text":"消息发出去了～ 不过 OAuth 授权需要你在**飞书里点击并完成登录授权**，光说\"同意\"可能还没生效 😄\n\n你试试点一下飞书里我刚发的链接，看看能不能跳转到授权页面完成授权？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":32347,"output":271,"cacheRead":26328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58946,"cost":{"input":0.0097041,"output":0.0003252,"cacheRead":0.0015796799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01160898}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776179420711,"responseId":"062d8bdca4e1fbbaebb7cea5f54743ab"}}
