{"type":"message","id":"81134be7","parentId":"3c86453b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:12:59.077Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still expired. The user sent a message but that didn't refresh the token. The issue is that the user access token is stored in Keychain and it expired. I need to ask them to do the OAuth flow properly.\n\nLet me think about this - the feishu channel in OpenClaw should be handling the OAuth automatically when they interact. But the user token in Keychain is expired and needs to be refreshed via the OAuth flow.\n\nMaybe I should tell them to check if they got an authorization card in Feishu that they need to click. Or perhaps the issue is something simpler - let me check if there's a feishu_oauth_batch_auth tool mentioned in the MEMORY.md.\n\n\nLooking back at MEMORY.md, it mentions that when I encounter token expiration issues, I should try refreshing or retrying at lower frequency first, and only bother the user if I can't resolve it myself. It also notes that when permission cards appear for im:message or im:message.send_as_user scopes, I shouldn't keep checking if the token is valid—the user has already granted batch authorization. This suggests there's a batch auth mechanism I should use instead of repeatedly trying the same approach.\n\nThe real issue is that bitable permissions are separate from message permissions, so even though the user authorized message access, that doesn't automatically grant bitable access. I need to guide them through authorizing specifically for bitable. The feishu_oauth_batch_auth tool mentioned in MEMORY.md might be what I should try calling to get the necessary permissions in one go.","thinkingSignature":"958939461720c0651b273db7f575bbf64bf509e38d766bbf9b42ba298deebcb3"},{"type":"text","text":"还是过期 😔 消息发了但 token 没刷新——问题是你之前给我授权的是**发消息**的权限，但读写 bitable（错题本）需要单独授权。\n\n我来调一下批量授权试试：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ii0e3qfo8pic_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"comm