{"type":"message","id":"efed8d50","parentId":"c932ab28","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:16:37.612Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying \"你自己想办法解决，我同意的\" - they're telling me to figure it out myself, they've given consent. They want me to find a way to refresh the token without requiring them to click on a web link.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The issue is that the user access token (UAT) is stored in the macOS Keychain and it's expired. The refresh token flow typically happens automatically through the OAuth flow, but if the refresh token itself has expired or is invalid, we need a new authorization.\n\nHowever, maybe I can look at this from a different angle:\n1. Can I use the app-level token instead of user-level token for bitable operations?\n2. Is there a way to trigger a token refresh through the existing OpenClaw infrastructure?\n\nActually, looking at the MEMORY.md notes:\n- \"遇到 token 过期 → 先自己尝试刷新或降频重试，实在搞不定再找频哥人工授权\"\n- \"飞书权限卡片处理（2026-04-03 新增）：当出现权限申请卡片时，不要反复排查token是否有效，直接建议用 feishu_oauth_batch_auth 重新授权\"\n\nSo there's a mention of `feishu_oauth_batch_auth`. Let me check if this is available as a tool or command.\n\nActually, looking at the error and the situation - maybe I should try using the feishu app scopes tool to check current permissions, and then see if there's a way to use app-level tokens for bitable operations.\n\n\nThe feishu_bitable_* tools might rely on app tokens rather than user tokens for certain operations, so let me verify the current app permissions first. According to MEMORY.md, the feishu plugin has a health check script at ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/feishu-plugin-health.sh that might help diagnose the issue, and the plugin health check runs every 30 minutes - so perhaps there's a mechanism already in place to handle token refreshes.\n\nLooking at the error code 99991677 more carefully, it's an authentication token expiry issue. Since the user is telling me to handle it myself but is unavailable to click authorization links, I should check if there's an existing refresh mechanism in the OpenClaw feishu extension that I'm missing. The tools feishu_app_scopes and feishu_bitable_get_meta are showing as available in the function list, so let me try calling those to see if they work and what permissions are actually configured.\n\nMy approach will be to first verify what permissions are currently granted by calling feishu_app_scopes, then attempt feishu_bitable_get_meta with the app token to see if app-level permissions are sufficient for reading the bitable, and if that fails, check if the feishu plugin has a built-in auto-refresh mechanism I can leverage.","thinkingSignature":"3384bb2d0b45bc7f1b68a3591985162c7cc0c45038f953fda942f6d21f2859af"},{"type":"text","text":"好，我来想办法。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tc5v1q6okawk_1","name":"feishu_app_scopes","arguments":{}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":17,"output":601,"cacheRead":61066,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":61684,"cost":{"input":0.0000050999999999999995,"output":0.0007212,"cacheRead":0.0036639599999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.004390259999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776179778433,"responseId":"062d8d42bb764f8de22d15ffa23b8057"}}
