{"type":"message","id":"6940b4b7","parentId":"9f2c3d1c","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:17:31.990Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's an appSecret! Let me try to get a new user access token by using the app credentials and the existing refresh token.\n\nActually, the standard OAuth flow for user tokens requires:1. Authorization code (from the user clicking the auth link)\n2. Exchange code for token (done server-side with app credentials)The refresh token is stored in the keychain but the UAT is expired. The refresh token itself should still be valid if it hasn't expired.\n\nLet me try to manually refresh the user token using the refresh token from keychain.\n\nActually, let me first check what's in the keychain for the feishu UAT entry.","thinkingSignature":"c4306ae26fe57393d7d47808bae997e007b16ebe0de960891dce384fc26753f3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_os988w97ah2e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"FULL_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s \"openclaw-feishu-uat\" -a \"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\" -w)\necho \"$FULL_TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('userOpenId:', d.get('userOpenId','')); print('has accessToken:', bool(d.get('accessToken',''))); print('has refreshToken:', bool(d.get('refreshToken','')))\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39768,"output":282,"cacheRead":26328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66378,"cost":{"input":0.011930399999999999,"output":0.0003384,"cacheRead":0.0015796799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01384848}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776179843006,"responseId":"062d8d830b023d2a91d2c040527b07fc"}}
