{"type":"message","id":"33560678","parentId":"e94e38b1","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:17:54.724Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The refresh token is not found. This might mean the refresh token has expired or been revoked. This is a common issue with OAuth tokens - the refresh token might have a longer lifetime but eventually expires.\n\nGiven this situation, I need to get a new authorization from the user. Since the user can't click the web link, let me think of alternatives:1. Can I trigger the authorization from within Feishu?2. Is there a mobile-friendly auth flow?3. Can I use the feishu bot DM to trigger auth?Actually, looking at this from a practical standpoint - the user is telling me \"你自己想办法解决\" but the reality is that OAuth tokens require user interaction to refresh. There's no way around this without user action.Let me be honest with the user about the situation and explain that while they said they同意, the technical mechanism requires them to click a link or interact with an authorization flow. I should offer alternatives.","thinkingSignature":"274057dec0fab32c62515d3f0a6298ae4c971dc07b2994591d99c641234cc8c8"},{"type":"text","text":"频哥，技术实话跟你说 😅\n\nOAuth 的 refresh_token 已经失效了（可能是过期了），这个不是\"同不同意\"的问题，而是 token 本身已经作废了，需要重新走一遍授权流程。\n\n**目前能解决的方式只有一种**：在飞书里打开授权链接并点击同意。\n\n你说打不开那个链接——可能是飞书内置浏览器限制。你能试试：\n1. 把链接复制到**手机浏览器**（Safari/Chrome）里打开\n2. 或者在**电脑微信**里点击那个链接\n\n如果实在都打不开，我先把 Q4 这道题**先记录下来**，等下次授权好了再录也行，不急～"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":40664,"output":327,"cacheRead":26328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67319,"cost":{"input":0.012199199999999999,"output":0.0003924,"cacheRead":0.0015796799999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.014171279999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776179862757,"responseId":"062d8d962f2d5bc14c78e56322261ba5"}}
